{"question_id": "8a2466db", "spans_supplied": 15, "request_sha256": "2246786e3fae7199ccf8f6c88dbe596aac433936ea1e24609b6bc3984eb8caed", "timestamp": "2026-10-07T09:08:57.740122+00:00", "status": "ok", "result": {"answer": "Here are some concrete places/areas to start learning more about video editing (based on our prior conversation):\n\n- Adobe Premiere Pro: focus on learning the Timeline panel (customizing tracks, track heights, track patching, clip grouping) — it’s the heart of editing.  \n- Performance/workflow: learn how Premiere Pro’s render cache works and how to manage it (Render Cache settings in Preferences) to improve playback and export performance.\n\nIf you want, I can expand this into a short learning path (beginner→intermediate→advanced), list specific tutorials or YouTube channels for Premiere Pro, or suggest exercises/projects to practice these skills.", "abstained": false}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3265, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 352, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 192}, "total_tokens": 3617}, "response_id": "resp_02e6b8640ede6402016ac60c2efb1087d0abf67e7d4a531306", "model": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "seconds": 4.696903399657458}
