{"question_id": "d24813b1", "spans_supplied": 15, "request_sha256": "6e398d083a42168e75d1b4daf7f82db84052ac854fffb858b2ee5304e2428b0f", "timestamp": "2026-10-07T09:08:56.074749+00:00", "status": "ok", "result": {"answer": "A few easy crowd-pleasers based on what you’ve asked about before:\n\n- Chewy chocolate chip cookies: a classic that’s easy to bake in batches. Tips from your earlier session — space cookies about 2 inches apart, bake ~10–12 minutes until lightly golden, then remove while still slightly soft and let cool on the baking sheet for 5 minutes before moving to a rack. Don’t overbake if you want a chewy center.\n\n- Oatmeal raisin (with nuts): a slightly heartier, “healthier” cookie option you mentioned wanting to try. Add chopped nuts for texture and swap part of the sugar for a little honey or brown sugar if you want a less-sweet profile.\n\n- Pound cake with bright/citrus elements: if you want something not cookie-based, a simple pound cake is a good make-ahead option; serving it with a citrus glaze or fresh citrus keeps it refreshing and offers contrast to richer bakes.\n\nGeneral party baking tips: pick 1–2 items so you’re not overwhelmed, bake things that travel well (cookies/pound cake), and stagger baking so everything isn’t coming out at once. If you want specific recipes (chewy cookie recipe, oatmeal-raisin with nut proportions, or a citrus pound cake), tell me which and I’ll share one.", "abstained": false}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2930, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 525, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 192}, "total_tokens": 3455}, "response_id": "resp_0f29163501e4af10016ac60c2d4ac087d0a1bfed2a0f142ea6", "model": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "seconds": 10.744787099771202}
